    "rapid_leap": 9
  },
  "technical_note": "Both hands contain separately notated voices. Keep the sustained upper and bass notes quieter than the moving inner lines. The LH moves to treble clef for bars 6\u20138 and returns to bass at bar 9. The full hand spans stay within an octave; the high climax asks for balance rather than force.",
